2025-09-30 21:00:19,492 [WARNING] Skipped idx=179: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='Supporting sentence: In humans, three TAp73 isoforms (TAp73α, TAp73β, and TAp73γ) have been identified. These isoforms are generated through the use of different promoters and alternative splicing, resulting in proteins with varying N-termini but all containing the central DNA binding domain and the C-terminal transactivation domain. The distinct N-termini may influence their subcellular localization, interaction with other cellular components, and overall function. Studies have shown that these TAp73 isoforms can act as tumor suppressors and are involved in various cellular processes, including apoptosis, cell cycle regulation, and angiogenesis. They are also implicated in the response to DNA damage and chemotherapy, particularly in the context of BRCA1-associated ovarian carcinoma, where they contribute to the chemosensitivity mediated by platinum-based therapies.'
2025-09-30 21:00:19,492 [WARNING] Skipped idx=180: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='Supporting sentence: In humans, three TAp73 isoforms have been identified: TAp73α, TAp73β, and TAp73γ. These isoforms are generated through alternative splicing of the TP73 gene and differ in their N-terminus sequences. They are known to play roles in various cellular processes, including apoptosis and cell survival, and their interactions with other p53 family members, such as p53, have been studied for their potential impact on tumorigenesis.'
